{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":139073,"duration_api_ms":138007,"num_turns":3,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"cf9b7a20-9bfd-4f8d-bebc-688d2b3624ac","total_cost_usd":0.47742305000000007,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":26294,"cache_read_input_tokens":79794,"output_tokens":2770,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":26294,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":2770,"cacheReadInputTokens":79794,"cacheCreationInputTokens":26294,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.2735045,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000},"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":102,"outputTokens":6544,"cacheReadInputTokens":1037678,"cacheCreationInputTokens":53863,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.20391855,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"rulings":[{"amendment_id":"fr-5-0fe11abb","decision":"accept","rationale":"The amendment correctly identifies that CleanFilter deletes microbe biomass without explicit handling — the four guild biomasses are multiplied down and the removed mass has no explicit destination. However, the fix recommendation must be nuanced. Reviewer 2 correctly notes that ROUTING.md (lines 146, 163) documents CleanFilter as a 'maintenance export' — mass intentionally leaves the system — and the before/after snapshot mechanism does capture the loss as out_mg in the BudgetEntry delta. So the mass is not truly 'unaccounted' in the ledger; it is implicitly recorded as an export. Nevertheless, the amendment is accepted because: (1) relying on implicit snapshot inference for a deliberate export is fragile compared to the explicit routing every other biomass path uses, (2) there is no named export ledger entry distinguishing CleanFilter export from other mass changes in the same tick, and (3) the open-system exclusion disables conservation checking for the entire tick, which could mask real imbalances from other processes running in that same tick. The correct fix is NOT to route biomass to dissolved organics (that would contradict ROUTING.md's export semantics), but rather to record an explicit, labeled export entry in the budget ledger so the mass removal is tracked with purpose and quantity, and ideally narrow the open-system guard suppression so it only exempts the CleanFilter stage rather than the whole tick."}],"summary":"Accepted fr-5-0fe11abb with an important caveat: the amendment's primary fix suggestion (route to dissolved organics) contradicts ROUTING.md which documents CleanFilter as an intentional maintenance export. The before/after snapshot mechanism does capture the mass loss, so the mass is not entirely unaccounted. However, the implicit-only tracking is fragile engineering — explicit export ledger entries would be more robust and would allow the conservation guard to verify the rest of the tick's processes. The fix should add explicit export tracking, not reroute mass to in-tank pools. The 2-1 reviewer consensus (plus planner) favoring accept, combined with the code's reliance on implicit snapshot inference for a deliberate design-level export, tips the balance toward acceptance."},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"1ef4b046-97f9-4d5a-a758-7eab917cdaf6"}
